# .oo Size Burn-Down Inventory
File: openOODA/audit/oo_size_2026-09-23.oot
Date: 2026-09-23
Status: inventory — no source splits yet

## Goal

Baseline per-file size and mixed-domain signals for every .oo file in
oodac, oodar, std, and the governance repo, so future source splits
have a worst-offenders-first burn-down list. Read-only scan; nothing
under oodac/, oodar/, or std/ was modified.

## Probe

qa/lint_oo_size.sh (134 lines, <= 256 ceiling). Per file: function
count (pub fn + fn at line start), longest function in lines by
brace-depth match (name included), mixed-domain signal = capability
tokens from >= 2 substrate groups (fs, net, gpu, thread, ffi, mem,
env, time). Thresholds: lines>256 (BIGFILE), fns>15 (MANYFN),
longest>80 (LONGFN). MIX is informational and never fails the probe.
Exit 1 while any size violation exists.

## Summary

files_scanned: 6817
rows_listed: 610
violations: BIGFILE=1 MANYFN=253 LONGFN=262 files_with_size_violation=514
mix_signals: MIX=130

Per-repo flagged rows (flagged / size-violation / mix):

- oodac: 141 / 93 / 60
- oodar: 2 / 0 / 2
- std: 465 / 420 / 66
- openOODA (governance): 2 / 1 / 2

Note: oodac/tests/fixtures/boundary_257_lines.oo is a deliberate
ceiling-test fixture, not a split candidate.

